// LEGAL POSITIONING NOTE — READ BEFORE EDITING. THIS IS THE MOST
// RESTRICTIVE COUNTRY IN OUR EUROPEAN COVERAGE:
// The 2010 Education Act (Skollagen 2010:800, effective 2011) allows
// fulfilling skolplikt outside school only on "synnerliga skal" —
// exceptional grounds — applied, in the law's own preparatory works,
// "with great restrictiveness". Religious and philosophical reasons
// are EXPLICITLY excluded; curriculum preference does not qualify.
// In practice hemundervisning is not permitted for compulsory-age
// children resident in Sweden. Families who have attempted it have
// faced vite (fines) documented at SEK 30,000-150,000 plus social
// services reports, and dozens have emigrated — most famously to
// Aland. Sweden shares with Germany the most restrictive framework
// in Europe.
//
// NEVER position Smartious as a legal homeschool route for
// compulsory-age children resident in Sweden. It would be commercially
// convenient and factually wrong. The honest positioning has three
// legs, all genuinely real:
//
// 1. SUPPLEMENTARY alongside a Swedish school enrolment — the largest
//    use case during ages 6-16 (Cambridge trajectory maintenance,
//    STEM extension, mother-tongue English academics).
// 2. POST-16 PRIMARY DELIVERY — skolplikt ends after year 9, around
//    age 16, and gymnasiet is VOLUNTARY. A 16-18-year-old in Sweden
//    is under no schooling obligation: full-time live A-Levels are
//    legally unproblematic. The cleanest post-16 window of any
//    restrictive country we serve.
// 3. The residence scope of skolplikt, stated factually: it applies
//    to children resident in Sweden (7 kap. 2 §), not to children
//    durably abroad — relevant to Swedish diaspora and internationally
//    mobile families. State the law; never coach circumvention.
//
// MARKET NOTE: Sweden's distinctive problem is QUEUES, not fees —
// voucher-funded bilingual schools (notably the Internationella
// Engelska Skolan chain) carry years-long waiting lists at little or
// no fee, while the fee-charging internationals run approximately
// SEK 150,000-250,000/year. Relocating families squeezed between the
// two are a core audience.
